{
 "priority": 7,
 "source_bins": [
  "talk.bin"
 ],
 "strings": {
  "Oh, Motomura-kun. It's that time already? Sorry to make you rush.": "",
  "I'll be leaving now, Yagami-san, so I hope to see you again soon!": "",
  "Yeah, same here.": "",
  "(A successful manager is one who puts his customers first... that way both parties win. Sounds like a great president.)": "",
  "You're Yagami-san, yes? I just wanted to say thank you for talking to the president whenever he's here.": "",
  "Umm, you were...": "",
  "Muramoto-san?": "",
  "...I'm Motomura. President Ichinose's secretary.": "",
  "Right, right, Motomura-san. You're always rushing in here to find the president even though you're nearly out of breath.": "",
  "Motomura-san?": "",
  "That's right, I'm President Ichinose's secretary.": "",
  "You're always rushing in here to find the president even though you're nearly out of breath.": "",
  "Motobayashi-san?": "",
  "Murabayashi-san?": "",
  "Yes, the president is a very... diligent man who often vists the stores to check up on them.": "",
  "Is that so? What a hardworking guy.": "",
  "Wait, you're by yourself today, Motomura-san?": "",
  "Yes, I am. The president told me I should watch and observe as well... He said I might learn something.": "",
  "That's why I've been standing here like this all day long.": "",
  "Hmm. I wonder why he'd tell you something like that.": "",
  "Beats me... All I know is I don't have time to be loafing around here like this...": "",
  "If I'm not around, then who's gonna manage the president's busy schedule? Only I have the knowhow to make it all work.": "",
  "Sounds like planning the president's every move is more complex than it would seem.": "",
  "Yeah, and thanks to me, the company's still running in the first place... *sigh*": "",
  "Motomura-kun. I'm sorry, but you're mistaken.": "",
  "...Huh? That voice...": "",
  "Whoa! Since when did you get here!?": "",
  "Motomura-kun, haven't you heard this saying?": "",
  "\"To whom you owe your gratitude can be cause for peace or strife.\"": "",
  "Do you understand the meaning behind this, Motomura-kun?": "",
  "To whom you owe... Who even says \"whom\" these days?": "",
  "You see, Motomura-kun, I appreciate your hard work every day. You always go above and beyond.": "",
  "Thank you for that.": "",
  "N-No, it's my pleasure.": "",
  "...But you shouldn't only credit yourself, either.": "",
  "Gratitude is best when shared with others, not only kept for yourself.": "",
  "You mustn't forget about everyone else who makes this business possible.": "",
  "I wanted you to realize this by looking at the way our staff members work...": "",
  "...You're right. Lately I've just felt so busy that all I could focus on was myself... Sorry for what I said.": "",
  "Oh, there's no need to apologize! I'm just glad you understand where I'm coming from.": "",
  "Yes. From here on out, I'll be turning over a new leaf.": "",
  "Indeed you will! That's why I'm having you relocate to this branch for a month, effective today!": "",
  "Okay, I'll—": "",
  "...Wait, whaaaat!?": "",
  "Remember how inspired you were today? That passion will help you survive the monotonous hell that is customer service!": "",
  "Besides, working like this builds character! Wouldn't you agree?": "",
  "...More like build stress.": "",
  "I learned a lot from you, President Ichinose. Gratitude is best shared with others... Those are wise words.": "",
  "Ah, it's little more than common sense.": "",
  "Now that Motomura-kun has learned this for himself, I'm sure it will refine his character a bit.": "",
  "Mm, I think so too.": "",
  "This may sound odd, but I sometimes see myself as a parent rather than a president.": "",
  "Not only do I want my employees to be happy with what they do, but I also want to see them mature and grow as people...": "",
  "Though I'm sure not all of them feel the same way. Ha ha ha!": "",
  "Well I'd say it's fine either way.": "",
  "Thanks, Yagami-san.": "",
  "...Oh <font_kind=yakuza_italic>that's</font_kind> not good!!": "",
  "What happened!?": "",
  "I forgot! I have an important meeting today!": "",
  "Motomura-kun usually keeps track of my schedule...": "",
  "Maybe he really is the driving force of the company!": "",
  "Ahaha...": "",
  "Well, see you later, Yagami-san! Oh, and please come back and enjoy our steaks again!": "",
  "Sure thing. Take care.": "",
  "(There he goes... He really had a strong presence about him. Hope he gets to his meeting in time.)": "",
  "(Now I'd better be careful where I place my gratitude... Well, I'm thankful for these steaks, for one.)": "",
  "Hey everyooooone! Sorry to interrupt, but I have an important announcemeeeent!": "",
  "My name is Yurika Tachibana, and I have some exciting news!": "",
  "If you're a mahjong lover, then you might just wanna stick around!": "",
  "The all-new Tachibana Mahjong has officially opened their doors to the public! So come on down to Nakamichi Alley!": "",
  "Not only can you enjoy the thrill of fast-paced, high-level mahjong, you can even play with the exciting Wear Me rule!": "",
  "So, I hope y'all stop by and play a game at our place sometime! Tee-hee!": "",
  "We'll be waaaaiting!": "",
  "(A new mahjong parlor at Nakamichi Alley, huh... What is this \"Wear Me\" rule, though?)": "",
  "(I should check it out sometime...)": "",
  "(...But man, that girl sure has guts, walking into a rival store and blatantly advertising her own like that...)": "",
  "Oh, you're the girl that came to the mahjong parlor the other day...": "",
  "That's right! Yurika Tachibana, at your service!": "",
  "Yurika! Eureka! You found meeeee! ♪": "",
  "Hey, don't just ignore me!": "",
  "You... had mentioned something about a new mahjong parlor?": "",
  "Oh! Yes, there is! It's called Tachibana Mahjong! Please, please, come on in!": "",
  "Wow, it looks pretty fancy in here.": "",
  "Hehe, why thank you!": "",
  "You said you can play using a special rule here? Wear Me, wasn't it?": "",
  "Yes! It's actually called \"wareme.\" The one who breaks the wall will pay and receive double.": "",
  "Double! So it's a high-risk, high-return rule. Sounds interesting.": "",
  "Maybe I should try it out...": "",
  "Yes, you should! And after you win, you can teach me some of your super-special-awesome moves!": "",
  "Uh... sure? I wouldn't mind explaining them, at least.": "",
  "Good, 'cause a lot of these mahjong terms have, like, uber hard-to-pronounce words. So I just make up names for them.": "",
  "Haha, well, I can get behind that.": "",
  "Tee-hee, I'm so glad you understand me!": "",
  "Oh, and may I have your name?": "",
  "Yagami-san, got it! I hope we can be good friends!": "",
  "Whenever you want to play, go talk to the people sitting at the tables.": "",
  "So how's the Wear Me rule treatin' you?": "",
  "Oh, Yurika-chan. It's actually really exciting. Thrilling, even.": "",
  "Reeeaaally? I'm so glad to hear it!": "",
  "I really wanna see you win with \"wareme.\"": "",
  "Haha, okay. I'll do my best.": "",
  "Then I'll be looking forward to it! Please come agaaain!": "",
  "Yagami-san, you did it! You're amazing!": "",
  "What can I say, I was just having a good time.": "",
  "You're really good at mahjong, though! That's so cool!": "",
  "Nah, I just got lucky.": "",
  "Now now, don't be so modest.": "",
  "Next time, can you win with a Pin Who?": "",
  "Pin Who...?": "",
  "Yeah! It's an \"all sequences hand\" that's worth 0 \"fu.\" Welp, I'm looking forward to it!": "",
  "Amazing, Yagami-san! You totally did the Pin Who!": "",
  "I think you mean \"pinfu.\"": "",
  "Aww, come on. Isn't Pin Who more catchy?": "",
  "I'd say it's more painful.": "",
  "Well, to each his own! I guess you learn something new every day, though!": "",
  "Please take this as a thank-you present!": "",
  "Yagami-san, can you do a Toy Toy next?": "",
  "Toy Toy?": "",
  "Yeah! It's also referred to as \"all triplets.\" At least I know that much!": "",
  "Yagami-san, make sure to win with a Pin Who next time!": "",
  "Amazing, Yagami-san! You actually did the Toy Toy!": "",
  "I think going with \"all triplets\" is a lot easier to understand.": "",
  "Huh? You really think so?": "",
  "Ehehe. Well. Since you fulfilled my request, I'll give you this as a present!": "",
  "Yagami-san, please do a Honey Sue next!": "",
  "Honey Sue?": "",
  "Yeah! Another word for it would be \"half flush.\" Does that help?": "",
  "Yagami-san, can you do a Toy Toy next? Or... all triplets. Whatever.": "",
  "Amazing, Yagami-san! You totally did a Honey Sue!": "",
  "...It's \"honitsu.\"": "",
  "Darn! I knew you wouldn't like it!": "",
  "Haha, well, your nicknames are pretty funny. I think you should keep using them.": "",
  "Tee-hee. Well, since you handled my request, I'll give you a li'l present!": "",
  "Yagami-san! Please do a Churning Potato next!": "",
  "Churning Potato?": "",
  "Yeah! Another word for it is \"nine gates.\" At least I know that much!": "",
  "Yagami-san, please win with a Honey Sue! Or \"honitsu\"! Whatever you wanna call it!": "",
  "Wow! That really was a Churning Potato! Amazeballs!": "",
  "You mean a \"chuuren poutou.\" More importantly, I need to visit a temple or something...": "",
  "Nine Gates is a really rare hand. You need to use up all the luck you have in order to get it...": "",
  "It's said that once your luck runs out, you'll end up... jinxed. That's why people go to a temple to get purified.": "",
  "Wow, really? I didn't know I was asking you to do something so tough...": "",
  "Then I'd better give you a special thank-you gift! Please, take this!": "",
  "Thanks for always taking my requests, Yagami-san!": "",
  "Come back and visit any time you want!": "",
  "Sure, I'll see you around.": "",
  "I'll be waitiiiiing!": "",
  "Yagami-san, please win with a Churning Potato! Or nine gates! Whatever you wanna call it!": "",
  "Oh, Yagami-san! Welcome. Hope you win big today!": "",
  "Hey there, Yagami-san! I hope you'll enjoy the \"wareme\" rule today.": "",
  "Yagami-san, you look like you'll rake in the points today!": "",
  "Just a gut instinct!": "",
  "Instinct!?": "",
  "Tee-hee, hope you win big!": "",
  "Ooh, Yagami-san, Yagami-san. Is there really a scary hand called Slew Uncle?": "",
  "That's \"suu ankou,\" also known as \"four concealed triplets.\" It's a yakuman hand.": "",
  "Boooooring. I thought it was a hand that causes your uncle to... you know, bite the dust.": "",
  "That's... ridiculous.": "",
  "Hi, Yagami-san! I've been working on my impersonations lately!": "",
  "What's this all of a sudden?": "",
  "Here, I'll give you my best one!": "",
  "*horse whinny* ": "",
  "So!? What do you think?": "",
  "Uh... I think it's pretty good?": "",
  "Yay! Woo-hoo! Yippee!": "",
  "<color=white>${value}</color> more spaces left to reach the goal!\nNow make like a cat on a hot tin roof and scurry on over!": "",
  "(Perfect. The wire's still fine too.)": "",
  "(Bah, the wire broke. Won't be able to use that one anymore.)": "",
  "(This calls for a wire. I should have <t:item_have_num=judge_thumbturn_wire> left.)": "",
  "(This calls for a wire... Which I'm out of at the moment.)": "",
  "(Doesn't look like I have a key for this door...)": "",
  "(Oh, looks like Tomioka-san left me some food. I believe this is... <t:prg_set=0>.)": "",
  "Someone sent me something...": "",
  "Guess what, Senpai! I stayed up all night prepping this presentation, and it is gonna go <font_kind=yakuza_italic>great</font_kind>!": "",
  "All night? Man, no wonder you stink. How're you supposed to present the new bento set smelling like rancid ass?": "",
  "What!? I do? Oh no... the presentation's in only ten minutes!": "",
  "...I'd say it's over already.": "",
  "Don't you start feeling lonely around this season, Senpai?": "",
  "Lonely? You just got paid, man. Why don't you go and buy some \"company\"?": "",
  "...Why would buying a company help? Besides, I don't think I could run one all by myself.": "",
  "You know that new girl, Nishiyama? The cute one all the guys in our department were talking about?": "",
  "Oh, her. Yeah, I heard she's popular. But she has a boyfriend outside of the company.": "",
  "Yeah, I know. But someone saw her hugging Tachioka-san on the stairs.": "",
  "Get outta here! Really? I thought Tachioka-san was married...": "",
  "I'm tellin' you, Miharu-chan was definitely smiling at me!": "",
  "That's the girl from Mijore, right? Of course she smiled at you—you're her customer.": "",
  "Nah, it wasn't just any smile... She <font_kind=yakuza_italic>locked eyes</font_kind> with me, Senpai! For like half a second!": "",
  "I think she might be into me!": "",
  "I think you don't know what you're talking about...": "",
  "You know Hanae-chan from Smile Burger? The one with the really bright smile?": "",
  "You really have a thing for servers, huh?": "",
  "There's a girl who sings at Theater Square pretty often. So I was listening to her and then she starts talking to me...": "",
  "She... thanked me from the bottom of her heart... with the most sincere smile I've ever seen...": "",
  "Somehow I just couldn't take it. Looking at her reminded me of a time before I became a completely shitty person...": "",
  "Guess her beautiful smile and your ugly soul were incompatible, Senpai.": "",
  "Apparently the boss is really going for Kiriko-chan, the girl who works at M Side Cafe.": "",
  "I can see why, she's a nice girl. Sweeter than the sweets she makes.": "",
  "Word. I wish she'd bake something just for me...": "",
  "This total rando comes up to me at Senryo Avenue, right? I guess she was a prophet of doom or something...": "",
  "Anyway, she goes up to me out of nowhere and tells me a \"falling calamity\" was about to befall me.": "",
  "That's some spooky shit. Maybe she was trying to con you into buying a talisman?": "",
  "Who knows. She creeped me the hell out, so I left as soon as I could.": "",
  "Hey Senpai, I saw this random dude who was cosplaying as Toya Tokunaga.": "",
  "Did he look like him?": "",
  "His outfit was perfect but... this guy was bald.": "",
  "Bald? Isn't Toya Tokunaga known for his lush, silky hair?": "",
  "Yeah, he missed the most important part.": "",
  "Yeah, so I'm more of a Wette Kitchen kinda guy. Smile Burger's way too manufactured, y'know?": "",
  "Hmm, how about Wild Jackson? Their ads have a lot of personality. Plus, their chicken's moist and tender.": "",
  "Oh, and have you tried the onion rings at Wette Kitchen? Dee-lish!": "",
  "We'd better stop before this turns into a Wette and Wild showdown...": "",
  "Haha, yeah.": "",
  "Senpai, they turned the area in front of the theater into a beer garden! Why don't we go there for First Friday!?": "",
  "Nope, Friday's the deadline, remember? I'll probably be doing overtime till the sun comes up.": "",
  "Dang. We'll never be able to say, \"Thank god it's Friday,\" will we?": "",
  "(I need a smoke. Wait... I'm out of cigs. Better hit the convenience store...)": "",
  "(I could use a smoke.)": "",
  "(Better get going.)": "",
  "Ugh... So exhausted...": "",
  "Ah, weren't you here before...? Hey, I noticed you're wearing some cordovans. I like your style.": "",
  "Thanks... I really wanted these, so I had to scrimp and save until I could finally afford 'em. How'd you know the material?": "",
  "Believe it or not, I had some decent shoes back in the day. Well... better hit the soup kitchen. See ya 'round, kiddo.": "",
  "...I wonder if he used to work at an office, too.": "",
  "Hey, it's you again. Man, you always look pooped.": "",
  "And you always look like you pooped yourself.": "",
  "Hah! True enough. But seriously, you oughta take it easy every now and then. For your health.": "",
  "Here. Warmth is the best cure for fatigue. Drink this and warm up your body and soul.": "",
  "Thanks... but this isn't hot at all! Well, I guess it'll help me buckle down and finish up the workday.": "",
  "Oh, hey Pops. Thanks for the coffee last time.": "",
  "You don't need to thank me. If anything, thank the dumpster behind the convenience store I found it in.": "",
  "...Seriously? Blech, no wonder I felt sick after that...": "",
  "Heh heh, sorry about that! I'll try to find something closer to the expiration date next time!": "",
  "I think I'll pass on that!": "",
  "Hey Pops, you said you had a pair of cordovans, right? What'd you used to do before you became homeless?": "",
  "Heh, I was a working man, just like you. Wore nice shoes, had a nice suit, scrambled all over town for business...": "",
  "Huh. Now that you mention it, you've always been a pretty bold guy.": "",
  "Heh, don't you get it? You need a bold attitude and balls of steel in order to get anywhere in life.": "",
  "There's a rumor that Kanrai serves special yakiniku to special customers.": "",
  "Yeah, that yakiniku's incredible. Wanna try it out sometime?": "",
  "Huh!? You've had it before? And are you offering to pay!?": "",
  "Naw, why do that when you can find it in the dumpster? Guess it's what you'd call \"aged meat.\" Gah hah hah hah!": "",
  "And here I was, about to take you seriously...": "",
  "Hey Pops, you ever heard about \"Dice & Cube\"? The ladies at the office are all talking about it these days.": "",
  "Apparently it's a game you play with virtual reality technology. I guess it's not up your alley...": "",
  "So they finished it after all... I thought it was impossible when I first saw the design document. I'll be damned.": "",
  "Wait... Pops, you used to be involved?": "",
  "Man, I'm hungry. Might stop by Kyushu No. 1 Star on my way home.": "",
  "Nice. They choose their ingredients well. Trust me, they're the real deal.": "",
  "Oh! Sounds like you know a lot about that place.": "",
  "Yeah, I can tell from the scraps. Each scrap has quite the distinguished taste.": ""
 },
 "ref_tm": {
  "Yeah, same here.": "เออ ฉันก็เหมือนกัน",
  "Thank you for that.": "ขอบคุณมากนะ",
  "What happened!?": "เกิดอะไรขึ้น!?",
  "Ahaha...": "อาฮ่าฮ่า..."
 }
}
